--- body ---
## Goal

`erg update` fetches the latest binary from the git-erg repo origin and replaces itself, when a network connection is available. No Go toolchain required on the user's machine.

## Behaviour

- `erg update` checks origin for a newer binary (compare commit SHA or file hash)
- If newer: downloads and atomically replaces the running binary, prints version info
- If already current: says so and exits 0
- If offline or origin unreachable: exits 0 with a notice (never hard-fails)

## Open questions

- Distribution mechanism: `git archive` / raw GitHub download / GitHub Releases asset?
- Version signal: embed current commit SHA at build time (`-ldflags "-X main.version=..."`)?

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg update` replaces the binary with the latest from origin when a newer version is available
- [ ] `erg update` is a no-op when already up to date
- [ ] `erg update` exits 0 and prints a notice when offline
- [ ] Version is embedded in the binary and reported by `erg version`
